{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/422004-hooks-based-on-classic-themes","id":422004,"title":"Hooks Based on Classic Themes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-27T11:44:51-08:00","id":422004,"title":"Hooks Based on Classic Themes","content":"So the motley has a new friend.She's somewhat of a celebrity really. She could be a singer or a model or a beauty pageant contestant. When she walks into the room she turns heads. She's well-respected and well-liked in the freehold. She's mastered a number of Fairest contracts, rarely makes a faux pax. Everything she does is controlled. She can work a crowd or influence people one on one. Her skill and beauty are almost unmatched....<b><i>almost</i></b>. That's where the motley comes in. Someone seems to be upstaging her. Now it's obvious she's cheating. She's a mere <i>mortal</i>. Let's be real here. There's something behind this. Who knows maybe she's using autotune? Maybe she uses a lot of padding. She could have gotten plastic surgery? Perhaps she even made a pledge with one of the Fairest's rivals to be more beautiful or more talented then she has any right to be.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just look into it okay.&quot; she says with a wink and a smile.<br /> <br /> Presumably they shadow her, they dig through her stuff, but nothing seems to be out of the ordinary. Just an ordinary lower class girl who works part time at the coffee shop and has dreams of making it as a starlet. Father is a plumber. Her mom works at the local diner. Yes, nothing unusual at all here. She hasn't even seen any other Changelings besides her little rival of course.<br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean <b>nothing</b> turned up? Haha that's okay I got mad for a sec. But there has to be <i>something. </i>Look into her family members. Maybe she has some connections, maybe she lipsyncs. It's alright. I'm sure you did your best. It's only a week or so until the contest.&quot; She says optimistically. She perhaps gives them a little something for their trouble, but the last line hints at her desperation.<br /> <br /> Once again, they find nothing in time. She loses the pageant, the record deal, the singing contest--whatever to her. She's not taking it well. Nobody at the freehold seems to have seen her for days despite normally being an outgoing person.<br /> <br /> &quot;No, that's not possible. She slept with the judges I bet. Or she's a loyalist in disguise trying to undermine us. You believe me don't you?&quot; she says pleadingly with tear filled eyes. So maybe they're convinced to take one more look into it. Maybe not. Either way, either directly or indirectly, she finds out that the motley has either given up or once again--nothing, squat, zero, zilch.<br /> <br /> &quot;That <b><i>whore. </i></b>She's turned them all against me! She clearly seduced one of them that awful skanky femme fatale. I'm a laughing stock of the entire freehold. All of my friends are against me now! She's turned everyone against me. That proves it! I was right! She'll pay for this! She and anyone who's ever talked to her. She has to go. Those traitors too. It's the only way everything will go back to normal. They'll love me again!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I couldn't find a thread where to put this, so I made one and put it here.<br /> <br /> It's supposed to resemble the clarity degeneration of a Fairest who is starting to realize she might not actually be the 'fairest one of all' </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3309-electrick","user":"electrick","date":". 02-27-2015, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3309-electrick","name":"electrick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T07:38:54-08:00","id":422902,"title":"","content":"It makes for a nice story but I have a really hard time buying a &quot;mere mortal&quot; beating out a fairest who can boost any relevant dice pool to superhuman levels. Luck of the dice can always throw a wrench but you won't see that coming in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:02:02-08:00","id":423199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>helel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/422004-hooks-based-on-classic-themes?p=422902#post422902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes for a nice story but I have a really hard time buying a &quot;mere mortal&quot; beating out a fairest who can boost any relevant dice pool to superhuman levels. Luck of the dice can always throw a wrench but you won't see that coming in advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I forgot to mention this, but she has the homebrew merits 'Blessed by the Dice Gods' as well as 'The Wyrd Doesn't Care How Big You Can Get Your Persuasion DP'. Unfortunately they're not available to players :/<br /> <br /> 'Blessed by the Dice Gods'<br /> Effects: This character can use weighted dice, in some cases even lying about the number of successes. I'm the ST--I'll get away with it<br /> <br /> 'The Wyrd Doesn't Care How Big You Can Get Your Persuasion DP'<br /> Effects: The character can declare an opposing character's rolls ineffective. It matters not how big they are. In fact rolls can be done away all together and the results may simply declared.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> :P<br /> <br /> You write as if I would actually need to make these rolls to 'justify it'. The implausibility is supposed to be part of the point.<br /> <br /> I can toy with or throw out the mechanics to suit my needs. I'm sure every WOD developer will back this up. If I really <i>needed</i> to, which I don't, but say I do I could always homebrew something to make it possible. It's an idea presented in the core fluff after all. The Fairest might not actually be the Fairest ones of all. The Wizend's mystical dodads don't last like when a human does it. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3309-electrick","name":"electrick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T12:48:28-08:00","id":423329,"title":"","content":"Well, if you're talking &quot;classic themes&quot;, then there's more than one way to be Fairest of Them All.<br /> <br /> I mean, why wait until you lose to start tearing someone down? Just slip a little extra milk in their coffee so they get extra phlegmy before her big song number.<br /> <br /> For that matter, if you can't beat 'em, make 'em join you as a backup singer. If she's really the nobody to start with, surely you can use a little Fleeting Spring and Vainglory to talk her into joining up with you. Keep Your Enemies Closer and all that. If things go well, her strengths are now your strengths, and if things don't work out, you've got plenty of fodder for figuring out how to arrange for her to have a bunch of &quot;compromising photographs&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T15:32:56-08:00","id":423494,"title":"","content":"Don't mind me. I'm a rivet counter. I break immersion any time something doesn't make logical sense. Through your whole story my brain was shouting &quot;the moral and the fairest probably have the same base stats and even a modest fairest can boost that to the tune of +4 to +8.&quot;<br /> <br /> My fix for that would be to have the mortal win the contest out of the blue. They just need one lucky die roll for that and after it doesn't matter that the fairest can perform better because they already lost and can't retroactively win. Hence bitterness and jealousy and requests to the PC's to &quot;look into&quot; the mortal. But that's just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T03:57:55-08:00","id":423950,"title":"","content":"The Wyrd is fate and destiny. A Changeling's fate and destiny is not their own, however much they might wish it to be, a mortal is intimately tied to the world as a still natural part of that world. She is part of the skein of fate and the Changeling is an interloper. The mortal is Fairest of them All because she is mortal, because she lacks contracts to bolster her, because she is <b>not</b> a Changeling. Therefore, when fighting fate, the NPC does not require any buff or any bolstering. Instead, the Fairest would receive a hefty penalty to her own dice pools, contracts may simply fail to work because the Wyrd isn't with her, catches and loopholes in the contract prevent it working in these very specific circumstances. This is a living narrative, these are some of the oldest stories ever told, and the Wyrd is the story so it won't change the story simply because you ask it to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 03-01-2015, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T04:08:22-08:00","id":423953,"title":"","content":"Can the True Fae love? Can they really care for a mortal? Any of the Lost would say no, but there's a story that's being kicked around. His name was Oliver, or was it Odell? Oisin? It began with an 'O' anyway. They say his Keeper came to him in the night and he fell in love with her. Oldest horror story in the book, right? Well get this... He goes off to live with her, but he gets home sick. She asks him, don't leave! She -asks-. She doesn't demand or throw a fit and tantrum, she doesn't rip him apart or change him. So he leaves, saying he'll come back. She even gives him a horse, but she gives him one warning, she says, &quot;Don't walk on the ground.&quot; He rides home and when he leaves the Hedge he emerges in front of a highway. The noise of the cars and the modern day shock him, he'd been gone hundreds of years. He got off his horse and aged three hundred years in a moment and died. Not before telling his story to a Changeling at the Hedge Door. Loyalist propaganda? Fantasy? Or maybe not all the Kindly Ones are misrepresenting the name! ...then again, maybe she delighted in seeing him die. Who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}